<title>EGYPT: Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</title>
<headline>Yield falls on Egyptian six-month T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on Egyptian 182-day treasury bills fell to 9.999 percent from 10.041 percent at the previous auction on January 13.</p>
<p>The Central Bank of Egypt announced the following details (values in pounds, previous auction in brackets):</p>
<p>Maturity date: July 19, 1997 (July 15, 1997)</p>
<p>Average yield: 9.999 percent (10.041)</p>
<p>Value of bids accepted: 903.675 million (709.575 million)</p>
<p>Value of bids: 1,160.275 million (771.275 million)</p>
<p>Range accepted: 8.987-10.061 percent (9.900-10.090)</p>
<p>Range of bids: 8.987-10.300 percent (9.900-10.555)</p>
<p>Number of bids accepted: 124 (85)</p>
<p>Number of bids: 151 (94)</p>
<p>$1 = 3.40 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo reporting unit +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
